  <itemBody><p>A reading item asks the student to select the author's claim inside a short paragraph.</p><hottextInteraction responseIdentifier="RESPONSE"><prompt>Read the paragraph and select the phrase that best states the author's claim.</prompt><p>The city should convert the vacant lot on Pine Street into a pocket park. <hottext identifier="A">A small green space would give nearby residents a shaded place to gather</hottext>, and volunteers have already offered to maintain native plants. <hottext identifier="B">The lot is 0.4 acres</hottext> and sits next to a bus stop. <hottext identifier="C">The planning department posted the proposal last Tuesday</hottext>. <hottext identifier="D">Two benches are stored in a public works warehouse</hottext>. </p></hottextInteraction></itemBody>
  <responseProcessing template="http://www.imsglobal.org/question/qti_v2p1/rptemplates/match_correct"/>
</assessmentItem>",
}
`;

